\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{ca8e886}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The build script writes the JVM launcher with the line the platform study arrived at: 8 compiler threads, transparent huge pages and a heap chosen by the engine that will run, a fixed 13 GB for every engine but the machine and at most 7 GB for the machine. The native image is built with the inline lists that the machine ships, with a fallback when the build environment lacks the tools to derive them, and the test kit is no longer part of a distribution. The arena build test passes on the tree with the new script: a clean copy, the 14 modules that ship compiled from source in the 8-CPU, 16 GB container, and the run line of the definition with 8 threads.}

\p{Detail: \src{docs/research/profiles/J1.md}, \src{docs/PLATFORM.md}. Commit \commit{ca8e886}. Session: [exactness](ses-874D). Related: [the decision on the JVM launcher line](dec-E3EX).}
